/** @mainpage WaveDataProvider Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section wavedataproviderintro WaveDataProvider Introduction

    The %WaveDataProvider module provides a data provider API for Wave accounting and invoicing services.

    Wave is a free accounting, invoicing, and receipt scanning software designed for small businesses.
    This module enables integration with Wave through its GraphQL API, supporting operations on:
    - Customers (create, read, update, delete, search)
    - Invoices (create, approve, send, search)
    - Products (create, read, update, search)
    - Accounts (create, search)
    - Transactions (create, search)
    - Sales Taxes (create)
    - Events/Triggers (invoice created)

    To use this module, use \c "%requires WaveDataProvider" in your code.

    @section wavedataproviderauth Authentication

    Wave uses OAuth 2.0 for authentication:
    - **OAuth 2.0**: Use oauth2_client_id and oauth2_client_secret for third-party applications.
    - **Full-stack Token**: For testing, use the \c token option with a Wave full-stack token.

    @par Example:
    @code{.py}
#!/usr/bin/env qore

%requires WaveDataProvider

WaveDataProvider provider({"token": ENV.WAVE_TOKEN});

# List all customers
AbstractDataProviderRecordIterator i = provider.getChildProvider("customers").searchRecords({"businessId": business_id});
while (i.next()) {
    printf("Customer: %s (%s)\n", i.getValue().name, i.getValue().email);
}

# Create an invoice
hash<auto> invoice = provider.getChildProvider("create-invoice").doRequest({
    "businessId": business_id,
    "customerId": customer_id,
    "invoiceDate": "2025-01-15",
    "status": "DRAFT",
});
printf("Created invoice: %s\n", invoice.id);
    @endcode

    @section wavedataproviderrelnotes Release Notes

    @subsection wavedataproviderv1_0 WaveDataProvider v1.0
    - Initial release of the %WaveDataProvider module
*/

#! Contains all public definitions in the WaveDataProvider module
public namespace WaveDataProvider {
    # AppName is defined in WaveDataProviderDefs.qc
}
